// Rolling hills — the procedural preset, with nothing built on it.
//
// A deliberate contrast to the showcase map: no river, no bridge, no mountain, and
// nothing that has to be crossed in a particular place. Terrain here is one smooth
// noise field, so movement is about distance rather than about finding the one way
// through.
//
// It exists mostly to prove that picking a scenario really does change the world. If
// this and the showcase map ever look alike, something is wrong with the selection and
// not with the terrain.
//
// Same file format as `config/world.ron` — this is a `MapSettings`, and everything in
// CONTENT.md about editing that applies here too.
(
    // Smaller than the showcase map. Nothing here needs the room, and a tighter grid
    // makes the difference between the two obvious the moment either loads.
    grid_radius: 9,

    // World height of one voxel level. Matched to the showcase map so a piece is the
    // same size on both and the two are honestly comparable.
    level_height: 0.4,

    terrain: Perlin((
        // Fixed, so this map is the same every launch. A random seed would make "did
        // the scenario change?" impossible to answer by looking.
        seed: Some(20260726),

        // Two octaves: broad hills, then a little roughness on top. One octave alone
        // reads as a smooth dome rather than as ground.
        steps: [
            (x_freq: 0.035, y_freq: 0.05, magnitude: 3.0),
            (x_freq: 0.11, y_freq: 0.13, magnitude: 1.0),
        ],
    )),
)
